+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** The game is unplayable for colorblind, motion-sensitive, and low-vision players (GDD E9; stories-v2 7.3): state colors collide under CVD, the pulse effects never rest, HUD chrome has no scale knob, and settings don't persist.
+
+**Approach:** Three colorblind palettes as first-class `palette.json` mode tables (simulator-derived, palcheck-oracled), a reduced-motion mode that pins the PULSE16 effects static while crisis readability survives on already-static channels, a ×1.00/×1.25/×1.50 UI-scale knob (user rulings 2026-08-19: disk persistence, settings panel, 3 steps), caption-strip completion over the 7.2 seam, and a settings PANEL (popover pattern, intent-parity) persisted to an app-side settings file. All View/app-lane — the sim never knows a11y exists.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Sim untouched [ODN-1]: no `core/` edits, no snapshot fields, no `LOG_VERSION`, no sim events; T1 + replay byte-identical (proven, not assumed).
+- Palettes are DATA: mode tables in `data/palette.json`; class colors remapped at draw time (catalog bytes fold `cat.hash` — `packet_types.json` is untouchable).
+- Every mode restyles ALL of the view: state triad, lanes, ghost, roofs/host/router tones, packet class colors, water/coast/park map tokens, wire ribbons/crisis outline.
+- palcheck extended: per-mode presence scans + a mechanical pairwise-separation check of the signal-token pairs under each deficiency's simulation.
+- Full input parity via the Intent layer for every new control (panel open, row navigate, row activate, scale step).
+- Panel labels ASCII-only (lint gate 6); bundled font only; settings I/O app-side with defaults fallback.
+- New T2 goldens are fresh demos/golden dirs, cause-documented; existing goldens byte-identical.
+
+**Ask First:**
+- Any pressure to touch `core/`, a snapshot field, or `LOG_VERSION` (a11y is View-only — a red flag, briefing scope guard).
+- A mode table that cannot separate a required token pair under simulation — halt with the measured deltas, never eyeball-tune canon.
+
+**Never:**
+- No difficulty options, control remapping, localization, TTS/screen-reader (follow-ups).
+- No `packet_types.json`/`balance.json`/catalog edits (golden-poison).
+- No continuous scale zoom; no font-glyph packet icons (the `icon` field stays [LATER]).
+- No new HUD surface besides the settings panel + a compact active-mode chip.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Enable deutan palette | panel row activate | whole frame restyles (map tokens + ribbons + class colors included); mode chip shows it | palcheck deutan leg green |
+| Reduced-motion + live crisis | R-equivalent on | ring + crisis outline widths static; banner/glyph/readouts unchanged | crisis readable in the a11y_reduced golden |
+| Scale ×1.50 at min window 1152×648 | panel stepper | top band (health card, forecast, crisis banner), QoS panel, tray, caption strip never overlap | layout clamps, AC-pinned |
+| Panel opens mid-run | settings intent | run pauses (if live); stays paused after close — explicit resume | pause chip reflects state |
+| settings.bin missing/corrupt | launch | defaults (palette off, motion on, ×1.00); a stderr note; rewrite on next change | never crash, never block launch |
+| palette.json mode table malformed | palette_load | base palette fallback (jcol precedent) | palcheck flags the mode loudly |
+| Muted audio + alert | 7.2 seam | caption strip still captions (muted ≠ silent) | existing contract, pin it |
+
+</frozen-after-approval>
+
